	abstract = {Leadership psychology and development reveal how leaders think, behave, and grow in ways that influence organizational performance and human wellbeing. Cognitive styles, emotional intelligence, motivation, and resilience interplay with structured development practices like coaching, feedback, and experiential learning. As workplaces become more complex, effective leadership is defined by the ability to adapt, foster psychological safety, and sustain health over time. Further exploration may highlight how leadership evolves across careers, emphasizing continuous development as a driver of long-term success and organizational effectiveness. Leadership Psychology and Development: Performance, Wellbeing, and Evolution explores how psychological factors shape leadership effectiveness, development, and decision-making in organizational environments. It examines the relationship between leadership performance, personal wellbeing, and continuous growth, highlighting how leaders evolve to meet changing demands while supporting individual and team success. This book covers topics such as emotional intelligence, organizational culture, and business communication, and is a useful resource for business owners, psychologists, academicians, researchers, and scientists. Coverage: The many academic areas covered in this publication include, but are not limited to: Administration & Leadership Business Communication igital Technology Educational Administration & Leadership Emotional Intelligence Employee Wellbeing Job Satisfaction Organizational Culture Organizational Development Psychology Workplace Culture. © 2026 by IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.},
	type = {Book},
